{
  "area": "props-vehicle-placement",
  "description": "Where a world vehicle is parked (PL.core-vehicle-rules, U106(3), U49(3); the Unreal P9e critic's M3): given its place's point, where the street is, the buildings' footprints, the statics a body cannot stand in, the villagers' slots and where everything E acts on stands, the parking spot and its tier, or a refusal with a code and the spot an engine that still draws the vehicle draws it at. Metres on core's ground plane (x, z); heights are y. Data in, decision out: no navmesh and no overlap test (the caller states the street and the statics). Owned by the vehicles pack (packs/vehicles). Ops: probes {at, radiusM} -> {points}; park VehicleParkingInput -> VehicleParking. Every case is {name, note?, op, input, expected}; numbers compare within tolerance, everything else exactly, object key sets included. Runner: src/props/vehicle-placement-corpus.ts. Regenerate with npm run vehicle-placement-corpus; npm run vehicle-placement-corpus:check fails on any difference.",
  "version": 1,
  "pack": "packs/vehicles",
  "sources": [
    "packages/core/src/props/vehicle-placement.ts (the rule) and src/props/vehicle-placement-corpus.ts (the runner)",
    "unreal feat/p9e-unreal a68b6d0, Source/InsimulRuntime/Private/InsimulVillageTraversal.cpp PlaceWorldVehicles 324–443 (the interim parking every constant is measured from, U106(3)); InsimulVillageDirector.cpp StreetPointNear 1663–1688; InsimulVillageProps.cpp AnyInteractableNear 1127–1139 and the farthest reach 404–420. Unreal's rule is not changed by this corpus",
    "packages/core/docs/traversal-systems.md §9b"
  ],
  "tolerance": 0.000001,
  "numerics": "Runners compute in IEEE-754 double precision (Unreal: double, as its FVector is). The tolerance covers reported numbers, not decisions: several cases decide exactly on a boundary (4.0 m from the place or a slot is far enough; 4.0 m from something E acts on is in reach; a static exactly 0.4 m off leaves room; a point 0.6 m outside a footprint is indoors), each exact in binary and in Unreal's whole centimetres.",
  "contract": {
    "units": "metres on the ground plane {x, z}; y is up; angles turn from +x toward +z (pickup-placement.json contract.frames)",
    "refusals": [
      "no-open-spot",
      "bad-place"
    ],
    "tiers": {
      "1": "every rule: open ground, clear of the slots, and nothing E acts on in reach of the spot or of any of its eight stands",
      "2": "open ground clear of the slots; nothing E acts on in reach of the spot (its stands need only be open)",
      "3": "open ground with nothing E acts on in reach of the spot; a villager's slot may be nearer than 4 m"
    },
    "constants": {
      "ringsM": {
        "value": [
          7,
          9,
          11,
          13,
          5
        ],
        "source": "VT:398 {700.0, 900.0, 1100.0, 1300.0, 500.0} cm, in that order"
      },
      "headings": {
        "value": 16,
        "source": "VT:400–403 K < 16, FRotator(0, 22.5 * K, 0)"
      },
      "snapM": {
        "value": 1.5,
        "source": "VT:403 StreetPointNear(…, 150.0, …) cm"
      },
      "snapStepM": {
        "value": 0.75,
        "source": "VD:1671 Ring * 75.0 cm"
      },
      "snapDirections": {
        "value": 8,
        "source": "VD:1673–1675 K < 8, 45 * K + 22.5 * (Ring % 2)"
      },
      "minFromPlaceM": {
        "value": 4,
        "source": "VT:408 Dist2D(Cand, Place) >= 400.0 cm"
      },
      "footprintMarginM": {
        "value": 0.6,
        "source": "VT:379 FVector(60, 60, 0) cm"
      },
      "bodyRadiusM": {
        "value": 0.4,
        "source": "VT:389 MakeCapsule(40.f, 88.f) cm"
      },
      "bodyLowM": {
        "value": 0.12,
        "source": "VT:388–389 100.0 - 88 cm"
      },
      "bodyHighM": {
        "value": 1.88,
        "source": "VT:388–389 100.0 + 88 cm"
      },
      "stands": {
        "value": 8,
        "source": "VT:410–415 Q < 8, 45.0 * Q"
      },
      "standM": {
        "value": 2.5,
        "source": "VT:412 * 250.0 cm"
      },
      "slotClearM": {
        "value": 4,
        "source": "VT:417 >= 400.0 cm"
      },
      "reachMarginM": {
        "value": 0.5,
        "source": "VP:1131 InteractReachCm + 50.0 cm"
      },
      "reachM": {
        "value": 4,
        "source": "VP:417–419 the largest of props.contract rangesM and doorPromptRadiusM (props/interactables.json), plus reachMarginM"
      },
      "fallbackM": {
        "value": 8,
        "source": "VT:436 StreetPointNear(Place, 800.0, Street) cm"
      }
    },
    "probes": "the street search round a point out to radiusM: the point itself, then ring r = 1, 2, … while 0.75 · r <= radiusM (+1e-9), each with eight points at 0.75 · r m, heading 45° · k plus 22.5° on odd rings, k = 0..7",
    "park": "place or groundY not finite -> bad-place. For tier 1, 2, 3, for each ring of ringsM in order, for heading k = 0..15 (22.5° · k): the ring point is moved to the first probe within snapM that is on the street (absent streets: everywhere; an area holds a point on or inside it); none -> a street miss. The spot is closed when it is nearer the place than minFromPlaceM, indoors (inside a building footprint grown by footprintMarginM on each side along its own axes, inclusive; a circle by its radius), or not open (a static whose height band, absent or meeting groundY + bodyLowM .. groundY + bodyHighM, lies strictly within bodyRadiusM), or any of its eight stands (standM away, heading 45° · q) is indoors or not open. It is not quiet when anything E acts on stands within reachM (<=) of it, or, in tier 1 only, of any stand. It is not clear of the slots when a slot is nearer than slotClearM. Closed -> a closed miss; else not quiet -> an interactable miss; else not clear of the slots and tier < 3 -> a slot miss; else taken: {ok, at, tier, ringM, heading, distanceM, misses}. No tier takes a spot -> {ok: false, code: no-open-spot, at: the first street probe within fallbackM of the place (onStreet true), else the place itself (onStreet false), distanceM, misses}. misses counts every turned-away candidate over all tiers",
    "when": "an engine parks each world vehicle nobody drives at its registry location's place, at world start and after every load; a driven vehicle follows its driver; one got off stays where it was left until the next load. Each vehicle is parked on its own (two at one place get the same spot: Unreal's rule as it stands, docs/traversal-systems.md §9b)",
    "deviations": [
      {
        "id": "refuse-when-nothing-open",
        "unreal": "no tier finds a spot: the vehicle stands at the street by the place itself (StreetPointNear 8 m), or the place's point, logged \"NO open spot\" (VT:431–436)",
        "core": "refuses with `no-open-spot`, carrying that same spot as `at` (and `onStreet`)",
        "why": "the ruling's shape asks for a decision or a refusal with a code; an engine that still draws the vehicle draws it at `at`, as Unreal does"
      },
      {
        "id": "stated-streets",
        "unreal": "a street point is the navmesh point a probe projects to (60 x 60 x 80 cm box) that lies on a road band or paving (OnStreet; VD:1663–1688)",
        "core": "the caller states the street as areas (`streets`) or passes `isStreet`; the spot is the probe point itself",
        "why": "core has no navmesh; the probe pattern (rings 0.75 m apart, eight ways, odd rings turned half a step) is core's"
      },
      {
        "id": "stated-footprints",
        "unreal": "a building's footprint is the world-aligned bounds of its colliding components, grown 60 cm on X and Y (VT:372–383)",
        "core": "the caller states each footprint as a box (`at`, `half`, `axis`) or a circle, grown 0.6 m along its own axes (a circle by its radius)",
        "why": "meshes and transforms are the engine's; for a box on the world axes the two agree"
      },
      {
        "id": "open-as-cylinder",
        "unreal": "open ground is no WorldStatic overlap with a capsule of radius 40 cm and half-height 88 cm centred 100 cm up (VT:386–390)",
        "core": "no stated static within 0.4 m (strictly) of the spot whose height band meets 0.12–1.88 m above the ground; a static with no band always meets it",
        "why": "the capsule's rounded ends are the engine's shape; the statics are stated, not overlapped"
      },
      {
        "id": "one-ground-height",
        "unreal": "the overlap is tested at each candidate's own navmesh height",
        "core": "the band is read at the place's ground (`groundY`) for every spot",
        "why": "core works on (x, z) with no terrain, as pickup-placement.ts does"
      },
      {
        "id": "panel-open",
        "unreal": "AnyInteractableNear answers true everywhere while a props panel is open (VP:1132), so a load with a panel open finds no tier's spot",
        "core": "an open panel is not read: only where things stand",
        "why": "where a vehicle is parked does not depend on what the player has open"
      }
    ],
    "sourceAbbreviation": "VT = unreal a68b6d0 Source/InsimulRuntime/Private/InsimulVillageTraversal.cpp; VD = …/InsimulVillageDirector.cpp; VP = …/InsimulVillageProps.cpp"
  },
